{"id":"oil","name":"Oil","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:oil","torrey:oil"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Oil","text":"Only olive oil seems to have been used among the Hebrews. It was used for many purposes: for anointing the body or the hair (Ex. 29:7; 2 Sam. 14:2; Ps. 23:5; 92:10; 104:15; Luke 7:46); in some of the offerings (Ex. 29:40; Lev. 7:12; Num. 6:15; 15:4), but was excluded from the sin-offering (Lev. 5:11) and the jealousy-offering (Num. 5:15); for burning in lamps (Ex. 25:6; 27:20; Matt. 25:3); for medicinal purposes (Isa. 1:6; Luke 10:34; James 5:14); and for anointing the dead (Matt. 26:12; Luke 23:56). It was one of the most valuable products of the country (Deut. 32:13; Ezek. 16:13), and formed an article of extensive commerce with Tyre (27:17). The use of it was a sign of gladness (Ps. 92:10; Isa. 61:3), and its omission a token of sorrow (2 Sam. 14:2; Matt. 6:17). It was very abundant in Galilee. (See OLIVE.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8081","lemma":"שֶׁמֶן","xlit":"shemen","gloss":"grease, especially liquid","kjv":"anointing, fat, fruitful, oil","count":57,"share":0.59},{"strong":"H8492","lemma":"תִּירוֹשׁ","xlit":"tîyrôwsh","gloss":"must or fresh grape-juice","kjv":"wine","count":12,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H3323","lemma":"יִצְהָר","xlit":"yitshâr","gloss":"anointing","kjv":"anointed oil","count":11,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H4888","lemma":"מִשְׁחָה","xlit":"mishchâh","gloss":"unction","kjv":"anointed, ointment","count":11,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H5561","lemma":"סַם","xlit":"çam","gloss":"an aroma","kjv":"sweet","count":8,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H1715","lemma":"דָּגָן","xlit":"dâgân","gloss":"increase","kjv":"corn, wheat","count":9,"share":0.09}],"verses":["Exod.25.6","Exod.27.20","Exod.29.7","Exod.30.24","Exod.30.25","Exod.30.31","Exod.31.11","Exod.35.8","Exod.35.15","Exod.35.28","Exod.37.29","Exod.39.38","Lev.2.4","Lev.2.5","Lev.7.10","Lev.14.10","Lev.14.21","Lev.24.2","Num.4.16","Num.15.4",